VI  - 12
IP  - 4
DP  - 2019 Apr 5
TI  - Post-traumatic bronchobiliary fistula.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2018-228294 [doi]
LID - e228294
AB  - Post-traumatic bronchobiliary fistula (BBF) is a rare entity, with only a few 
      cases reported worldwide. Bilioptysis is pathognomonic of the condition, however, 
      bronchoscopy and bronchoalveolar lavage along with CT are used for confirmation. 
      We describe this condition in a young woman who presented to us with bilioptysis 
      following a laparotomy for blunt torso trauma. Diagnosis was made of BBF, 
      followed by surgical management and complete recovery. We emphasise the signs of 
      early diagnosis, confirmatory tests, individualised treatment and advocate 
      surgical management as the gold standard of treatment.
