TI  - Congenital lobar emphysema: diagnosis and treatment options.
PG  - 921-928
LID - 10.2147/COPD.S170581 [doi]
AB  - Although congenital lobar emphysema is a rare lung disease, it can cause severe 
      respiratory distress in the newborn. Lobectomy can be difficult because of the 
      hyperinflated lobe and limited space to carry out surgery. During the past two 
      decades, conservative treatment options have increased for patients with mild and 
      moderate disease.
