TI  - Transbronchial lung cryobiopsy in the diagnosis of interstitial lung disease.
PG  - 300-306
LID - 10.5578/tt.69078 [doi]
AB  - Transbronchial cryoprobe lung biopsy (TBCLB) have recently been introduced as a 
      safe diagnostic tool in the diagnosis of interstitial lung diseases. While we do 
      not enough evidence its role and place as a diagnostic procedure, the technique 
      has been adopted by many centers. In spite of expanding body of literature, there 
      are variations in patient selection and procedural aspect of the procedure. It 
      has been established as a safe procedure if safety measures are practiced. 
      Diagnosis of interstitial lung diseases continuous to be challenging. Surgical 
      lung biopsy considered as gold standard but its morbidity and mortality limit its 
      utilization in every case. Multidisciplinary medical decision is a validated team 
      work effort when approaching patients with interstitial lung disease.
