TI  - Airway Histopathology of Adolescent Survivors of Bronchopulmonary Dysplasia.
PG  - 215-218
LID - S0022-3476(19)30426-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jpeds.2019.04.006 [doi]
AB  - Long-term survivors of bronchopulmonary dysplasia develop chronic obstructive 
      lung disease. Herein we report in vivo histopathology from bronchial biopsies of 
      3 adolescent survivors of severe bronchopulmonary dysplasia. Thickened basement 
      membranes with lymphocytic infiltrates and signs of immature neoangiogenesis in 
      the absence of T-helper lymphocytes or eosinophils suggest the presence of an 
      ongoing active airway process.
