TI  - [Clinical approach to foreign body aspirations in children and legal results].
PG  - 136-141
LID - 10.5578/tt.68442 [doi]
AB  - Foreign body aspirations are a serious respiratory condition that can threaten 
      life, particularly in childhood, in the first three years of life. In our 
      article, the approach observed in physicians who face foreign body aspirations in 
      the pediatric age group are analyzed and the approach proposed in these cases are 
      discussed under the current literature and relevant legal regulations.
