TI  - [A woman with a rash after bronchoscopy].
LID - D3624 [pii]
AB  - A 69-year-old woman underwent bronchoscopy because of a suspected lung tumour. 
      Within 2 hours after bronchoscopy, the patient developed facial purpura. Based on 
      clinical assessment and histopathological images, we established the diagnosis of 
      post-bronchoscopy purpura. This is a benign, self-limiting complication. Within 5 
      days after bronchoscopy, the purpura disappeared.
