TI  - Combined Management of a Bronchial Artery Fistula After Lung Transplantation.
PG  - e99-e101
LID - S0003-4975(19)30916-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2019.05.028 [doi]
AB  - A 46-year-old female patient exhibited massive endobronchial bleeding after 
      dilation of a left bronchial anastomotic stenosis after lung transplantation, 
      consistent with a bronchopulmonary artery fistula (BPAF). The BPAF was treated 
      with a bronchial covered self-expandable metallic stent and percutaneous 
      transcatheter pulmonary artery stent placement. BPAF is rare and leads to death 
      in most cases because of massive hemoptysis. We describe a case of successful 
      combined management of BPAF using both bronchial and pulmonary stent placement.
