TI  - [Segmentectomy for Congenital Left Upper Lobar Bronchial Atresia].
PG  - 1001-1004
AB  - A 22-year-old woman visited a hospital to treat her dyspnea which had lasted for 
      some months. Chest X-ray showed hyperlucency in her left upper lung field and 
      chest computed tomography suggested left upper bronchial obstruction with mucoid 
      impaction. She was referred to our hospital for further examination and 
      treatment. Bronchoscopy showed left upper lobar bronchial atresia. Considering 
      her dyspnea worsened in relatively short terms, surgical treatment was chosen and 
      the resection of left upper division was successfully performed.
