TI  - A 53-Year-Old Man Presenting With Diplopia and Cavitary Lung Nodules.
PG  - e107-e112
LID - S0012-3692(18)32608-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2018.10.021 [doi]
AB  - A 53-year-old Chinese man presented with 1 week of worsening diplopia and 
      left-sided facial droop. His symptoms developed during a readmission for elective 
      drainage and curettage of a perianal abscess that recurred despite drainage 
      2 weeks before. He denied having other neurologic symptoms, and did not report 
      any cough, sputum production, night sweats, or fever. He was a lifelong nonsmoker 
      with a history of polymyositis treated with mycophenolate mofetil for the last 4 
      years. He had undergone surgical resection for jejunal adenocarcinoma 12 years 
      prior to this presentation. No evidence of recurrence was detected on 
      surveillance gastrointestinal endoscopies and CT scans.
