TI  - A rare cause of wheezing in a child with pulmonary atresia.
PG  - 449-451
LID - 10.4103/aca.ACA_92_18 [doi]
AB  - The determination of the exact cause for symptomatic airway obstruction in 
      pediatric patients not responding to medication can be a clinical dilemma. Very 
      rarely external vascular compressions can produce airway obstruction symptoms 
      unresponsive to usual bronchodilator medications. The successful management of a 
      child with pulmonary atresia and an innominate artery compression syndrome with 
      respiratory compromise due to tracheal compression is described.
