TI  - Unmasking of left upper lobe bronchial atresia in a case of H1N1 pneumonia.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2019-229820 [doi]
LID - e229820
AB  - We describe a case of H1N1 pneumonia with left upper lobe bronchial atresia. 
      Although bronchial atresia as an isolated occurrence is an innocuous finding, but 
      when it is superimposed by another major insult, it can amplify the disease 
      effect and can have adverse implications leading to significant morbidity. This 
      report highlights the fact that anatomical anomalies can be the cause of 
      inordinately severe or prolonged course of acute respiratory infection in 
      children.
