TI  - Radial probe endobronchial ultrasound (R-EBUS) guided transbronchial cryobiopsy 
      in the diagnosis of peripheral solitary pulmonary nodule.
PG  - 349-351
AB  - Solitary pulmonary nodule (SPN) always raises suspicion for early lung cancer, in 
      which accurate and less invasive biopsy is needed. We report a case of 
      transbronchial cryobiopsy of right upper lobe SPN under radial endobronchial 
      ultrasound (R-EBUS) guidance after an inconclusive computed tomography guided 
      transthoracic needle aspiration. A diagnosis of Stage 1B adenocarcinoma of the 
      lung was made. Patient subsequently underwent curative right upper lobectomy 
      after ruling out mediastinal lymph node involvement. To the best of our 
      knowledge, this is the first report of R-EBUS guided transbronchial cryobiopsy 
      case reported from Malaysia.
