DP  - 2019 Mar
TI  - Complete tracheal rings and hypoplastic left heart variant: a rare and fatal 
      association.
PG  - 445-447
LID - 10.1017/S1047951118002391 [doi]
AB  - Congenital complete tracheal rings are usually associated with pulmonary slings. 
      We report a rare association of congenital complete tracheal rings with 
      hypoplastic left heart variant. A term infant with diagnosis of a mildly 
      hypoplastic mitral valve, unicuspid aortic valve, and moderately hypoplastic 
      aortic arch with severe coarctation underwent a hybrid procedure initially. Upon 
      failing extubation attempts, complete tracheal rings were seen on direct 
      laryngoscopy. The combination of the lesions resulted in a poor outcome. In 
      patients with failure of extubation post-cardiac surgery, a diagnosis of complete 
      tracheal rings should be included in the differential and a direct laryngoscopy 
      should be considered.
