TI  - Successful Stenting for Bronchial Stenosis Resulting from Blunt Airway Trauma.
PG  - 3277-3280
LID - 10.2169/internalmedicine.0569-17 [doi]
AB  - Blunt airway trauma is rare but life threatening. Injuries to other vital organs 
      accompany this type of injury in most cases; therefore, conservative treatment 
      may be considered first. In cases of delayed fibrotic airway stenosis after 
      conservative treatment, surgical treatment or bronchoscopic intervention are 
      therapeutic options. We herein report a case of delayed airway stenosis after a 
      blunt traumatic airway injury that was successfully managed by silicone stenting.
