TI  - Bronchoscopic resection of a tracheobronchial leiomyoma in a pregnant patient.
PG  - 93-96
LID - S0959-289X(17)30293-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ijoa.2018.04.002 [doi]
AB  - Flexible bronchoscopy, therapeutic bronchoscopy and other procedures requiring 
      anesthesia are generally avoided in pregnancy and postponed until after delivery 
      if possible. We report a case of a parturient with an abnormal chest radiograph 
      and mild obstructive symptoms of unknown etiology. At bronchoscopy, a tumor 
      associated with post-obstructive suppuration was found and excised using 
      electrocautery snare and cryotherapy, for restoration of airway patency. 
      Coordination between pulmonary, obstetric, anesthesia, neonatology and thoracic 
      surgery services was essential in ensuring success and the safety of the mother 
      and fetus.
