TI  - Airway Complications After Lung Transplantation.
PG  - 693-706
LID - S0272-5231(17)30076-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2017.07.010 [doi]
AB  - Airway complications remain a significant source of morbidity and mortality after 
      lung transplantation. The incidence of complications is wide-ranging depending on 
      the definition of the event, and there is still no universally accepted grading 
      system for airway findings after transplantation. Additionally, although surgical 
      technique and organ preservation have improved, other modifiable risk factors 
      remain unclear. The management is as wide-ranging as the definitions. A 
      multimodality approach is often needed with airway stenting reserved for 
      refractory cases and stent management by a transplant team with expertise in 
      placement and management of long-term complications."
