TI  - [Bronchial carcinoid tumor and recurrent pneumothoraxes].
PG  - 263-266
LID - S0761-8417(17)30092-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.pneumo.2017.08.007 [doi]
AB  - Pneumothorax is a rare clinical manifestation of lung cancer. It can 
      exceptionally reveal a bronchial carcinoid tumor. We present the case of a 
      27-year-old woman in whom recurrent pneumothoraxes were the clinical 
      manifestation of a bronchial carcinoid tumor. The interest for chest computed 
      tomography and bronchoscopy to identify etiology of secondary pneumothoraxes will 
      be discussed.
