TI  - Aortopexy for Life-Threatening Airway Obstruction Following Division of Double 
      Aortic Arch.
PG  - NP66-NP68
LID - 10.1177/2150135117709023 [doi]
AB  - Symptoms of airway compression secondary to double aortic arch are relieved by 
      division of one of the two aortic arches. However, in some cases inherent 
      tracheomalacia and other factors may result in persistence of symptoms. We report 
      one such occurrence in our experience and describe the use of aortopexy as a 
      curative procedure to tackle this problem.
