PMID- 28689530
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20180320
LR  - 20180320
IS  - 1681-7168 (Electronic)
IS  - 1022-386X (Linking)
VI  - 27
IP  - 6
DP  - 2017 Jun
TI  - Congenital Vallecular Cyst: ARare and Potentially Lethal Condition.
PG  - 376-377
AB  - Congenital vallecular cyst is a rare laryngeal lesion, accounting for 10-20% of 
      all laryngeal cysts, with a potential to cause severe upper airway obstruction, 
      which can be fatal. It can cause stridor, apnea, cyanosis, respiratory distress, 
      and feeding difficulties. Diagnosis requires a high level of clinical suspicion 
      and helps in timely intervention. Direct laryngoscopy is gold standard for 
      definitive diagnosis. Treatment options include aspiration, marsupialization, and 
      surgical excision. Here, we report a case of 7-week-old infant with complain of 
      recurrent episodes of cyanosis when agitated, since the age of 3 weeks, admitted 
      with impression of apparent life-threatening events (ALTEs). Extensive 
      investigations were non-conclusive, which were done in local hospital. Direct 
      laryngoscopy was performed in our hospital and showed presence of a vallecular 
      cyst. Thus complete excision of cyst was done in the same setting with dramatic 
      relief of symptoms.
