TI  - Endobronchial-Guided Vascularized Tissue Flaps for a Bronchopleural Fistula.
PG  - e1-e3
LID - S0003-4975(17)30239-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2017.01.104 [doi]
AB  - The management of bronchopleural fistulas can be challenging. The initial 
      treatment is usually conservative, but operative intervention with transposition 
      of vascularized pedicled flaps may be required in refractory cases. We present 
      the case of a 67-year-old man with stage IIIa squamous cell carcinoma of the lung 
      who underwent a lower and middle bilobectomy after receiving neoadjuvant 
      chemoradiation. His postoperative course was complicated by empyema and a 
      bronchopleural fistula. Because of difficulty accessing the fistula, 
      endobronchial-guided vascularized tissue flaps were successfully used to close 
      the fistula.
