TI  - Bronchoscopic and surgical management of rare endobronchial tumors.
PG  - 1093-7
LID - 10.4103/0973-1482.186692 [doi]
AB  - Pure endobronchial neoplasms are a rare entity, and they may present with diverse 
      pathological findings. Malignant diseases are more common than benign ones, and 
      they mostly originate from the surface epithelium. Endobronchial tumors usually 
      present with symptoms such as cough, hemoptysis, recurrent pneumonia, wheezing, 
      and chest pain. Flexible bronchoscopy is necessary for diagnosis and evaluation 
      of these endobronchial tumors. Advance bronchoscopy or definitive surgery is the 
      modality of treatment for these tumors based on the presentation. We present a 
      case series of patients suffering from different rare endobronchial tumors and 
      their management along with the review of literature.
