TI  - Conservative management of pediatric tracheal rupture.
PG  - E1-E3
LID - 10.1002/ppul.23507 [doi]
AB  - Traumatic injuries to the pediatric trachea are uncommon events that require 
      prompt diagnosis and management. When they do occur, tracheal injuries often 
      arise in the setting of high impact trauma and are accompanied by major injuries 
      to other organ systems. In this report, we present the diagnosis and conservative 
      management of tracheal rupture at the carina in an 11-year-old female with severe 
      intracranial injuries. Pediatr Pulmonol. 2017;52:E1-E3. © 2016 Wiley Periodicals, 
      Inc.
