DP  - 2016 Jul 4
TI  - Veno-arterial ECMO for rescue of severe airway hemorrhage with rigid bronchoscopy 
      after pulmonary artery thromboendarterectomy.
PG  - 242-4
LID - 10.5301/ijao.5000493 [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary endarterectomy (PEA) is the treatment of choice to relieve pulmonary 
      artery obstruction in patients with chronic thromboembolic pulmonary hypertension 
      (CTEPH). We present a patient with airway obstruction and acute respiratory 
      failure due to large blood clots obstructing the trachea and main left bronchus. 
      This condition was accompanied by right ventricle failure and cardiogenic shock. 
      A venoarterial ECMO system was used for cardiopulmonary support before extracting 
      the clots and clearing the airway by rigid bronchoscopy.
