DP  - 2016 Aug
TI  - EBUS-guided mediastinal lung cancer staging: monitoring of quality standards 
      improves performance.
PG  - 762-3
LID - 10.1136/thoraxjnl-2015-206985 [doi]
AB  - This audit examined key performance indices related to endobronchial ultrasound 
      (EBUS)-guided mediastinal lung cancer staging before and after the introduction 
      of defined quality standards, at four independent EBUS centres in one cancer 
      network. Data from 642 procedures were prospectively collected and analysed. The 
      introduction of standards was associated with a significant increase (p<0.001) in 
      sampling of key mediastinal lymph node stations (4R, 4L and 7) and a reduction in 
      the variability of staging sensitivity between centres. These data reinforce the 
      requirement for an appropriate regulatory framework for EBUS-transbronchial 
      needle aspiration provision that includes quality assurance and performance 
      monitoring.
