TI  - [A case report of a bronchial foreign body removal by direct laryngoscopy with 
      fiber bronchoscope].
PG  - 2089-90
AB  - An 11 year old girl presented with dyspnea and a rough cough, after having 
      mistakenly swallowed a steel ball and unable to relieve the symptoms. Chest X-ray 
      showed an image consistent with a 10 mm diameter circular object, embedded in the 
      right mainstem bronchi near the fifth thoracic level and the medicastinal moving 
      to the right. A clinical diagnosis based on these findings: foreign body of the 
      right bronchial.
