TI  - Right Lower Lobe Superior Segmentectomy in a Patient With a Displaced Bronchus.
PG  - e121-2
LID - S0003-4975(15)01345-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2015.07.085 [doi]
AB  - An 81-year-old woman with adenocarcinoma in the lower superior segment of the 
      right lung underwent superior segmentectomy of the right lower lobe through a 
      thoracotomy. Preoperatively, we detected an anomalous B10c bronchus branching 
      from the right lower superior segment bronchus with multiplanar reconstruction 
      computed tomography and virtual bronchoscopy. Intraoperatively, we stapled and 
      cut the right lower superior segment bronchus at the level of the peripheral 
      anomalous B10c bronchus under bronchoscopic visualization. Precise anatomic 
      understanding is very important for segmentectomy, especially in patients with 
      anomalous bronchi. Multiplanar reconstruction computed tomography and virtual 
      bronchoscopy are useful for preoperative planning.
