TI  - Effectiveness of bronchial thermoplasty in severe asthma in 'real life' patients 
      compared with those recruited to clinical trials in the same centre.
PG  - 267-71
LID - 10.1177/1753465815601332 [doi]
AB  - Published information on the effectiveness of bronchial thermoplasty (BT) for 
      severe asthma in 'real life' patients is limited. We compared safety and efficacy 
      outcomes 12 months post procedure in 10 clinic patients and 15 patients recruited 
      to clinical trials of BT at the same centre. Baseline asthma severity was greater 
      in the clinic group. Adverse events were similar. Clinical improvements occurred 
      in 50% of the clinic patients compared with 73% of the research patients.
