TI  - Guidelines update: Post-treatment follow-up of adult head and neck squamous cell 
      carcinoma: Screening for metastasis and metachronous esophageal and bronchial 
      locations.
PG  - 217-21
LID - S1879-7296(15)00085-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.anorl.2015.07.001 [doi]
AB  - OBJECTIVE: The present article is an update of the guideline of the French 
      Society of Otorhinolaryngology and Head and Neck Surgery (SFORL) on the 
      post-treatment follow-up of adult head and neck squamous cell carcinoma 
      concerning screening for metastasis and metachronous esophageal and bronchial 
      locations. METHODS: A multidisciplinary work-group was entrusted with a review of 
      the literature on the above topic. Guidelines were drawn up, based on the 
      articles retrieved and the work-group members' own experience. These were then 
      reviewed by an editorial group independent of the work-group. A coordination 
      meeting then finalized the guidelines. Guidelines were graded A, B, C or "expert 
      opinion" according to decreasing level of evidence.
