TI  - [Dynamics of morphologic changes in tracheobronchial system in patients with 
      acute carbon monoxide poisoning complicated by thermochemical damage to 
      respiratory tract].
PG  - 12-5
AB  - The authors identified three severity degrees of thermochemical damage to 
      respiratory tract during acute carbon monoxide poisoning. Follow-up bronchoscopic 
      studies were performed, and characteristic signs of thermochemical damage to 
      respiratory tract in acute carbon monoxide poisoning were diagnosed. Evidence is 
      that the signs were following certain sequence: from edema and hyperemia of 
      respiratory tract lining to severe purulent discharge.
