TI  - Long-term survival after pneumonectomy for primary pulmonary malignant melanoma.
PG  - 1428-30
LID - S0003-4975(14)01516-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2014.06.110 [doi]
AB  - As few as 30 cases of primary malignant melanoma of the lung have been reported 
      in the literature. Many patients die within months of diagnosis; few published 
      cases describe patients who survive long-term after treatment. We report a case 
      of primary pulmonary malignant melanoma in a patient who remains disease-free 60 
      months after pneumonectomy.
