DP  - 2015 Mar
TI  - Butyrfentanyl overdose resulting in diffuse alveolar hemorrhage.
PG  - e740-3
LID - 10.1542/peds.2014-2878 [doi]
AB  - Butyrfentanyl is a potent short-acting opioid and a fentanyl analog with 
      uncertain clinical effects. A review of the literature reveals no human case 
      reports of butyrfentanyl overdose. As the use of analog and synthetic drugs 
      continues to increase, clinicians are often faced with tremendous uncertainty 
      when they encounter patients exposed to these synthetic drugs. We describe, to 
      our knowledge, the first case of a butyrfentanyl overdose that resulted in 
      clinically significant hemoptysis, acute lung injury, hypoxic respiratory 
      failure, and diffuse alveolar hemorrhage. Complicating this case was a 
      false-positive urine drug screen for fentanyl. Clinicians who encounter fentanyl 
      exposures should be aware they may in fact be dealing with butyrfentanyl. As 
      little is known of butyrfentanyl and our patient suffered a significant pulmonary 
      hemorrhage, those who encounter butyrfentanyl exposures should monitor for 
      hemorrhagic complications.
