DP  - 2015 Feb
TI  - Lobular capillary hemangioma of the trachea.
PG  - 127-9
AB  - As a polypoid form of capillary hemangioma, lobular capillary hemangioma (LCH) 
      most commonly occurs on the cutaneous and mucosal surfaces and is frequently 
      benign in children. Tracheal LCH is a rare benign tumor in adults, with 
      hemoptysis being one of the most serious forms of presentation. A definite 
      diagnosis of LCH depends on its histopathology. In clinical practice, however, 
      radiological characteristics are an important component for making a suggestive 
      diagnosis. We present a case of tracheal LCH and describe its features on 
      computed tomography, pathology, and differential diagnosis. A review of the 
      relevant literature is also provided.
