TI  - [Hemoptysis in Pregnancy].
PG  - 244-248
LID - 10.1055/a-0853-0643 [doi]
AB  - Here we present an extremely rare but important cause of pulmonary hemorrhage 
      during pregnancy. A 41-year-old patient was seen with hemoptysis in the 29th week 
      of her pregnancy which was initially assessed as unspecific inflammation. At the 
      34th week of pregnancy, she presented again, this time with hemoptoe and 
      dizziness caused by an unknown idiopathic pulmonary AV malformation. The patient 
      underwent extensive interdisciplinary evaluation including bronchoscopy, 
      emergency cesarean section was performed, which was followed by CT scan and 
      VATS/minithoracotomy with segment resection.
