TI  - Analysis of Related Factors for the Retention Time of Tracheobronchial Foreign 
      Bodies in Pediatrics.
PG  - 262-267
LID - S0022-4804(18)30589-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jss.2018.08.024 [doi]
AB  - BACKGROUND: This study aims to investigate the related factors for the retention 
      time of tracheobronchial foreign bodies in infants and children, to provide help 
      for the assessment of the disease, surgical risk, and prognosis. MATERIALS AND 
      METHODS: The clinical data of 1060 patients with tracheobronchial foreign bodies 
      from January 2015 to December 2015 were retrospectively studied, and the 
      correlation of the retention time of foreign bodies with age, gender, 
      preoperative complications, granulation formation, operation time, and hospital 
      stay was analyzed. RESULTS: The retention time of foreign bodies was not 
      correlated with age (r = 0.041, P = 0.194) and gender (r = 0.039, P = 0.214) but 
      was correlated with preoperative complications (r = 0.072, P = 0.023), 
      granulation formation (r = 0.134, P < 0.001), operation time (r = 0.112, 
      P < 0.001), and hospital stay (r = 0.189, P < 0.001). CONCLUSIONS: The retention 
      time of foreign bodies was closely correlated with granulation formation, 
      preoperative complications, operation time, and hospital stay.
