TI  - Successful Excision of Endobronchial Cellular Schwannoma With Right Lower Sleeve 
      Lobectomy.
PG  - e203-e205
LID - S0003-4975(18)31241-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2018.06.088 [doi]
AB  - Cellular schwannoma is a rare variant of schwannoma, showing high cellularity and 
      a low mitotic index. A 64-year-old man was admitted to our hospital with a 
      2-month history of productive cough. Chest computed tomography showed an 
      endobronchial tumor with complete atelectasis of the right lower lobe. 
      Bronchoscopy showed an endobronchial tumor occluding the intermediate bronchus 
      that was diagnosed as a cellular schwannoma on biopsy and was successfully 
      excised with a right lower sleeve lobectomy to preserve the middle lobe. The 
      postoperative course was uneventful, and the patient remains well with no sign of 
      recurrence at the 7-year follow-up.
