TI  - Unnoticed aspiration of palate plate impression material in a neonate: Diagnosis, 
      therapy, outcome.
PG  - E58-E60
LID - 10.1002/ppul.23710 [doi]
AB  - A 7 week old infant was admitted with respiratory failure. Chest X-ray showed an 
      atelectatic right upper lobe, herniation of right middle and lower lobe into the 
      left thorax, and compression-atelectasis of the left lung. Thoracic CT showed 
      complete occlusion of the right superior bronchus with a radiopaque foreign 
      material. Six weeks prior, an impression for a palate plate using 
      polyvinylsiloxane was taken. The material was removed with a rigid endoscopy, in 
      readiness of extracorporeal oxygenation in case of tracheal obstruction or 
      bronchial rupture. After 4 months of follow-up a hyper reactive airway with 
      recurrent upper and lower airway infections remains.
