TI  - Bronchial Aspiration of Capsule Endoscope.
PG  - 122-125
LID - 10.1159/000453587 [doi]
AB  - Capsule endoscope aspiration is an increasingly reported complication, 
      potentially responsible for respiratory distress and asphyxia. This adverse event 
      is primarily managed by rigid bronchoscopy when spontaneous expulsion does not 
      occur. This complication is all the more detrimental to patients as it can delay 
      or jeopardize further digestive exploration. We report direct repositioning of 
      the capsule in the stomach at the same time as bronchoscopy, thus making 
      second-line gastrointestinal endoscopy needless.
