TI  - Computed Tomography Findings of Community-Acquired Stenotrophomonas Maltophilia 
      Pneumonia in an Immunocompetent Patient: A Case Report.
PG  - 961-964
AB  - Stenotrophomonas maltophilia (S. maltophilia) is a rare, but globally emerging 
      gram-negative multiple-drug-resistant organism usually found in a nosocomial 
      setting in immunocompromised patients. To our best knowledge, computed tomography 
      (CT) features of community-acquired S. maltophilia pneumonia have not been 
      previously reported in an immunocompetent patient. Herein, we presented the CT 
      findings of a previous healthy 56-year-old male with S. maltophilia pneumonia.
