TI  - Tracheal Resection for Symptomatic Tracheal Stenosis During Pregnancy.
PG  - 1589-91
LID - S0003-4975(15)01080-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2015.05.134 [doi]
AB  - A 31-year-old multipara was diagnosed with tracheal stenosis that developed after 
      intubation after an intentional benzodiazepine overdose in the first trimester of 
      pregnancy. Tracheal dilations only temporarily improved her dyspnea at rest. A 
      definitive repair by tracheal resection and reconstruction was performed at 28 
      weeks' gestation. Her symptoms resolved, and she delivered vaginally at 36 weeks' 
      gestation after spontaneous labor.
