TI  - [ENDOSCOPIC LUNG VOLUME REDUCTION IN PULMONARY EMPHYSEMA].
PG  - 609-16
AB  - Emphysema is characterized by an irreversible alveolar destruction, a progressive 
      lung hyperinflation and a dysfunction of respiratory muscles. It induces a 
      respiratory functional limitation and a decrease of quality of life. Endoscopic 
      lung volume reduction represents a potential alternative to surgical treatments 
      for advanced heterogeneous emphysema without concomitant surgical morbidity. The 
      different bronchoscopic systems for lung volume reduction currently under 
      evaluation are presented.
