DP  - 2015 Apr-Jun
TI  - Isolated Endobronchial Capillary Haemangioma: A Rare Cause of Haemoptysis in 
      Adult.
PG  - 109-11
AB  - Endobronchial capillary haemangioma is a very rare benign tumour in adults. The 
      clinical presentation and management of adult capillary haemangiomas involving 
      the tracheo-bronchial tree is not yet established. We present a case of an 
      isolated capillary haemangioma of the left main bronchus detected during the 
      evaluation of an adult male presented with haemoptysis. The lesion was managed 
      successfully bronchoscopically.
