TI  - Vanished: Is This for Real?
PG  - 367-9
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000168 [doi]
AB  - Spontaneous regression (SR) of lung cancer is especially rare. We report a case 
      of an early endobronchial squamous cell carcinoma that exhibited complete 
      radiologic and pathologic SR soon after diagnosis. The patient was monitored 
      radiologically and bronchoscopically at regular intervals and to date, the biopsy 
      samples have been negative. Remarkably, SR has been maintained 6 years after 
      diagnosis, without local recurrence or distant metastases. Many hypotheses abound 
      to explain how complete SR was achieved and maintained despite the lack of 
      treatment.
