PMID- 26059018
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20160630
LR  - 20150911
IS  - 1399-3038 (Electronic)
IS  - 0905-6157 (Linking)
VI  - 26
IP  - 6
DP  - 2015 Sep
TI  - Ground zero: not asthma at all.
PG  - 490-6
LID - 10.1111/pai.12421 [doi]
AB  - Upper airway obstruction is commonly misdiagnosed as asthma. We report on four 
      children with recurrent respiratory symptoms who had been erroneously diagnosed 
      as having asthma and who received anti-asthma medication for several years. The 
      evaluation of spirometry tracing was neglected in all cases. Subglottic stenosis, 
      tracheomalacia secondary to tracheo-esophageal fistula, double aortic arch, and 
      vocal cord dysfunction were suspected by direct inspection of the flow-volume 
      curves and eventually diagnosed. The value of clinical history and careful 
      evaluation of spirometry tracing in children with persistent respiratory symptoms 
      is critically discussed.
CI  - © 2015 John Wiley & Sons A/S. Published by John Wiley & Sons Ltd.
