TI  - Aorto-Tracheopexy in the Treatment of Hunter Syndrome.
PG  - 2190-2
LID - S0003-4975(14)01759-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2014.08.048 [doi]
AB  - Hunter syndrome is a multisystem genetic disease in which a significant 
      proportion of morbidity and mortality arise from respiratory dysfunction. 
      Notably, tracheal abnormalities in Hunter syndrome can compromise clinical 
      stability, and management is primarily supportive. We describe here the first 
      successful implementation of aorto-tracheopexy in a 19-year-old patient as a 
      surgical strategy to resolve progressive respiratory deterioration.
