TI  - Dyspnea on daptomycin: eosinophilic pneumonia.
PG  - 41-3
AB  - We present a case of drug-induced acute eosinophilic pneumonia with 
      characteristic imaging and bronchioloaveolar lavage (BAL) findings. Although not 
      a common diagnosis, it is important to consider in the right clinical scenario, 
      including a patient with presumed pneumonia that does not respond to typical 
      treatment. Diagnosis is confirmed by bronchoscopy with BAL. For drug-induced 
      types, treatment includes removal of the offending agent. Corticosteroids are 
      used if symptoms are severe and can result in rapid clinical improvement.
