VI  - 60
IP  - 9
DP  - 2015 Sep
TI  - Takotsubo Cardiomyopathy and Subsequent Seizures Induced by Flexible 
      Bronchoscopy.
PG  - e151-4
LID - 10.4187/respcare.03650 [doi]
AB  - Takotsubo cardiomyopathy is a transient left-ventricular dysfunction that 
      typically occurs in elderly women due to emotional or physical stress. An 
      85-y-old woman underwent flexible bronchoscopy to evaluate her malignant 
      lymphoma. After flexible bronchoscopy, she experienced takotsubo cardiomyopathy 
      diagnosed by left ventriculography and subsequent generalized tonic-clonic 
      seizure diagnosed by electroencephalography. Magnetic resonance imaging of her 
      brain after 1 d showed post-convulsive encephalopathy. We believe that these 2 
      consecutive incidents were caused by the physical stress of the flexible 
      bronchoscopy.
