TI  - Airway obstruction caused by penicilliosis: a case report and review of the 
      literature.
PG  - e25-8
LID - S0300-2896(14)00194-X [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.arbres.2014.04.015 [doi]
AB  - Penicilliosis is an opportunistic infection in HIV-infected and other 
      immunocompromised patients mostly in Southeast Asia, Southern China, Hong Kong, 
      and Taiwan, with respiratory manifestations in about one-third of patients. We 
      report the case of a 26-year-old non-HIV immunocompromised patient presenting 
      with an airway obstruction caused by penicilliosis, together with a review of the 
      literature of this rare condition.
