TI  - Mycobacterium avium pseudo-outbreak associated with an outpatient bronchoscopy 
      clinic: Lessons for reprocessing.
PG  - 106-108
LID - 10.1017/ice.2018.298 [doi]
AB  - We identified a pseudo-outbreak of Mycobacterium avium in an outpatient 
      bronchoscopy clinic following an increase in clinic procedure volume. We 
      terminated the pseudo-outbreak by increasing the frequency of automated endoscope 
      reprocessors (AER) filter changes from quarterly to monthly. Filter changing 
      schedules should depend on use rather than fixed time intervals.
