LID - bcr2018226074
AB  - Hyperimmunoglobulin E syndrome is a rare multisystem inherited disorder 
      characterised by high serum IgE levels, skin disorder causing eczema, dermatitis, 
      recurrent staphylococcal infections and pulmonary infections and various skeletal 
      and connective tissue abnormalities. Common presentation is with recurrent skin 
      and sinopulmonary infections. Several features unrelated to immune system such as 
      characteristic facial features, hyperextensibility of joints, multiple bone 
      fractures and craniosynostosis have been described in the literature. We describe 
      a rare presentation of this disease with invasive aspergillosis presenting as 
      mediastinal mass with extension to mediastinal structures and pulmonary 
      vasculature.
