TI  - Advanced Technologies for Imaging and Visualization of the Tracheobronchial Tree: 
      From Computed Tomography and MRI to Virtual Endoscopy.
PG  - 127-137
LID - S1547-4127(18)30005-7 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2018.01.005 [doi]
AB  - Advanced imaging plays an increasingly important role in the evaluation of the 
      trachea. The use of computed tomography (CT) has evolved to include multi-planar 
      reconstructions and 3-dimensional reconstructions for the evaluation of benign 
      and malignant disease of the trachea. Advanced applications of CT include dynamic 
      expiratory imaging for the diagnosis of tracheomalacia and virtual endoscopy as a 
      complementary or alternative examination to flexible bronchoscopy. MRI of the 
      trachea has limited applications but may see increased use in the future.
