TI  - Intentional tracheoesophageal fistula cannulation for gastric decompression in 
      type C esophageal atresia.
PG  - 367-369
LID - 10.1111/pan.13351 [doi]
AB  - We describe a nonsurgical technique for managing gastric distention in infants 
      with type C esophageal atresia, involving intubating the trachea with an 
      umbilical catheter and entering the stomach through the fistula as soon as a 
      flexible bronchoscope found its wide-open orifice. This technique might have a 
      special role when gastric distention precedes other commonly used preventive 
      measures.
