TI  - Proximal Left Main Bronchus Resection-Reconstruction through Left Thoracotomy 
      with Tracheal Traction.
PG  - 174-176
LID - 10.1055/s-0037-1603532 [doi]
AB  - Surgical approach for resection-reconstruction of the proximal left main bronchus 
      has been a matter of discussion. Through standard left thoracotomy, the proximal 
      main bronchus close to the carina is not easily exposed. Accordingly, median 
      sternotomy or right thoracotomy may be commonly employed, but the exposure and 
      management of the distal left main bronchus may be difficult through the 
      approach. Here, we present a left thoracotomy approach with traction of the 
      trachea, which may easily allow excellent exposure of the proximal end of the 
      left main bronchus and the carina.
