AB  - We describe a case of a man with ectopic Cushing's syndrome, elevated serum 
      beta-D-glucan, and respiratory cultures with Pseudomonas, Aspergillus, and a 
      partially acid-fast organism. Our case highlights challenges in diagnosis and 
      management of coinfection in an immunocompromised host.
