TI  - Management of Persistent Air Leaks with Intrabronchial Valves.
PG  - 603-606
LID - 10.1055/s-0037-1603622 [doi]
AB  - Persistent air leaks (PALs) are regarded as a frequent complication after 
      thoracic surgery resulting in prolonged hospitalization and increased morbidity. 
      Several more or less invasive therapeutic approaches are available for treatment 
      of PAL with varying degrees of success. The endoscopic placement of one-way 
      intrabronchial valves in the segment(s) in which the air leak has been located 
      offers a highly effective and well-tolerated minimal invasive option for patients 
      with PAL.
