VI  - 12
IP  - 4 Suppl
DP  - 2016 Oct-Dec
TI  - Transplant Pulmonary Interventions: Translating Lung Transplant Interventions to 
      Nontransplant Patients.
PG  - 18-20
LID - 10.14797/mdcj-12-4s1-18 [doi]
AB  - Roughly 10% of lung transplant recipients experience airway complications. 
      Although the incidence has decreased dramatically since the first lung 
      transplants were performed in the 1960s, airway complications have continued to 
      adversely affect outcomes. Bronchoscopic interventions such as balloon dilation, 
      airway stenting, and endobronchial electrocautery play an important role in 
      ameliorating the morbidity and mortality associated with these complications. 
      This review describes the array of bronchoscopic interventions used to treat 
      airway complications after lung transplant and how these techniques can be used 
      in nontransplant settings as well.
