DP  - 2016
TI  - Primary Mediastinal Large B-cell Lymphoma Exhibiting Endobronchial Involvement.
PG  - 3147-3150
AB  - Primary mediastinal large B-cell lymphoma (PMLBCL) is one of the subtypes of 
      diffuse large B-cell lymphoma. We experienced a rare case of PMLBCL that 
      exhibited endobronchial involvement. A 33-year-old Japanese female with the chief 
      complaints of epigastralgia, back pain, and nausea visited a primary care 
      hospital. Computed tomography of the chest and abdomen demonstrated a bulky mass 
      in the left anterior mediastinum, multiple pulmonary nodules, axillary lymph node 
      swelling, and a pancreatic tumor. Fiberoptic bronchoscopy showed a white-tinged 
      irregularly shaped endobronchial tumor accompanied by capillary vessel dilation 
      in the left upper lobar bronchus. Taken together, these findings resulted in a 
      diagnosis of PMLBCL.
