TI  - An Unusual Cause of Dyspnea.
PG  - e333-4
LID - S0003-4975(16)00235-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2016.02.051 [doi]
AB  - Sialadenoma papilliferum is a tumor of salivary gland origin. It is believed that 
      sialadenoma papilliferum is a benign lesion usually known to occur in the hard 
      palate, retromolar fat pads, lips, and parotid glands. Its origin in the 
      bronchial tree is an extremely rare occurrence. We report only the fourth known 
      case of bronchial sialadenoma papilliferum and the first to originate in the 
      trachea. The patient underwent successful resection of the lesion, with complete 
      relief of his dyspnea.
