TI  - Young man with dyspnoea for 6 months; presenting with subacute tracheal 
      obstruction due to leiomyoma.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2016-216096 [doi]
LID - bcr2016216096
AB  - Tracheal leiomyoma is a rare benign tumour with less than a 100 cases reported in 
      the literature. We report a case of leiomyoma initially presenting and being 
      treated as asthma until it lead to life-threatening tracheal obstruction, 
      requiring immediate surgical intervention.
