TI  - Massive Hemoptysis.
PG  - 139-47
LID - 10.1097/CNQ.0000000000000107 [doi]
AB  - Hemoptysis, or coughing of blood, oftentimes triggers anxiety and fear for 
      patients. The etiology of hemoptysis will determine the clinical course, which 
      includes watchful waiting or intensive care admission. Any amount of hemoptysis 
      that compromises the patient's respiratory status is considered massive 
      hemoptysis and should be considered a medical emergency. In this article, we 
      review introduction, definition, bronchial circulation anatomy, etiology, and 
      management of massive hemoptysis.
