TI  - Endobronchial valves in the management of bronchial fistulae caused by 
      bronchopulmonary aspergillosis.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2015-211955 [doi]
LID - bcr2015211955
AB  - Following an aggressive episode of bronchopulmonary aspergillosis, a 54-year-old 
      man developed a symptomatic air leak via a tunnel between the left upper lobe and 
      an extra chest wall cavity. Following the failure of several surgical procedures 
      to close the tunnel, endobronchial valves normally used in management of 
      emphysema were used to successfully treat the air leak.
