TI  - Mucosa-associated Lymphoid Tissue Lymphoma of the Trachea in a Patient with 
      Breast Cancer.
PG  - 2041-4
LID - 10.2169/internalmedicine.54.3925 [doi]
AB  - We herein report the case of a 93-year-old woman with breast cancer on the left 
      side. Preoperative computed tomography of the chest showed irregularities and 
      narrowing of the mid-trachea. Bronchoscopy was performed, and the results of a 
      biopsy supported a diagnosis of mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue (MALT) 
      lymphoma. The patient responded to treatment with prednisone alone, with a 
      reduction in the size of the lesion. MALT lymphoma of the trachea is extremely 
      rare, and there are only a few case reports of double cancer, i.e., MALT lymphoma 
      of the trachea and breast cancer.
