TI  - Bronchoscopic extraction of a chicken bone 5 years after aspiration.
PG  - E27-9
AB  - A 58-year-old man with a remote history of choking on a chicken bone 5 years 
      earlier presented with chronic cough but had no remarkable clinical examination 
      findings. He was being followed for recurrent pneumonias complicated by a 
      resistant empyema, for which he had undergone thoracotomy and decortication. 
      Imaging studies initially missed a foreign body (the chicken bone), which was 
      found on follow-up studies and was removed with a flexible bronchoscope despite 
      the fact that 5 years had passed since the aspiration.
