DP  - 2015 Jan-Mar
TI  - Disseminated penicilliosis marneffei in immunocompetent patients: a report of two 
      cases.
PG  - 161-5
LID - 10.4103/0255-0857.148433 [doi]
AB  - Disseminated penicilliosis marneffei is rarely seen in immunocompetent persons. 
      We report here two cases of disseminated penicilliosis marneffei in 
      immunocompetent hosts. Penicillium marneffei disseminated to the brain in one 
      patient and to the bone marrow in the other patient. Both patients received 
      amphotericin B liposome. The cases illustrate the importance of considering 
      penicilliosis marneffei as causes of systemic infections in immunocompetent 
      patients.
