TI  - A Successful Case of External Stenting for Bronchomalacia Lasting Over 20 Years.
PG  - e103-e104
LID - S0003-4975(19)30129-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2018.12.055 [doi]
AB  - We report on a patient with perimembranous ventricular septal defect and 
      pulmonary hypertension. He underwent pulmonary artery banding followed by 
      external stenting of the left bronchus because of secondary bronchomalacia. The 
      external stent applied was a ringed expanded polytetrafluoroethylene graft, 10 mm 
      in diameter and fixed at 8 points. Intracardiac repair was performed at the age 
      of 2 years and the external stent was left in place. Since then, the patient has 
      been healthy and computed tomography reveals that the external stent graft has 
      retained function for over 20 years.
