TI  - [Transbronchial cryobiopsies : a minimally invasive tool for the diagnosis of 
      interstitial lung disease].
PG  - 2079-2083
AB  - The diagnosis of interstitial lung disease (ILD) is challenging and relies on a 
      multidisciplinary discussion involving clinical, radiological and sometimes 
      histological features. Bronchoscopic lung cryobiopsies have emerged as a new 
      minimally invasive method of lung sampling and an alternative to surgical lung 
      biopsies. A good diagnostic performance and excellent safety profile make it an 
      interesting and worthful procedure which could decrease the number of patients 
      without proper diagnosis and treatment. There is a need for further studies to 
      standardize the technique in expert centers and to establish its role in the 
      diagnostic work-up of ILD.
