TI  - Optic Perineuritis Due to Tuberculosis.
PG  - 257-259
LID - 10.1097/WNO.0000000000000717 [doi]
AB  - A 30-year-old man experienced subacute peripheral visual field loss with 
      preserved central vision in his right eye. He was diagnosed with optic 
      perineuritis due to tuberculosis. Optic perineuritis is an uncommon disorder and, 
      at times, can be difficult to distinguish from optic neuritis. The 
      differentiation can have significant impact on diagnostic testing and patient 
      management.
