TI  - Endobronchial Non-Tuberculosis Mycobacterium Infection Presenting in a Healthy 
      Child.
PG  - 726-730
LID - 10.1177/0003489418784970 [doi]
AB  - OBJECTIVES: To describe a safe and effective treatment for endobronchial 
      Mycobacterium avium complex. METHODS: Case report and literature review. RESULTS: 
      We present a case of endobronchial M. avium complex in a healthy child treated 
      with serial carbon-dioxide laser excisions and antibiotic triple therapy using 
      azithromycin, rifampin, and ethambutol. No current guideline for the treatment of 
      these lesions in the pediatric population exists. CONCLUSIONS: In patients with 
      airway impingement, serial endoscopic surgical resection combined with 
      antibiotics can provide safe and effective management.
