AB  - Obstructive tracheal pseudomembrane is a rare complication of endotracheal 
      intubation, which could cause fatal airway obstruction following extubation. 
      Hereby, we reported a patient who had only undergone a short course of intubation 
      for a laparoscopic cholecystectomy and developed progressive respiratory distress 
      after extubation.
