TI  - Endobronchial Ablative Therapies.
PG  - 139-148
LID - S0272-5231(17)30119-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2017.11.008 [doi]
AB  - Endobronchial ablative therapies, such as mechanical debulking, laser therapy, 
      electrocautery, argon plasma coagulation, cryotherapy, brachytherapy, 
      photodynamic therapy, microdebrider bronchoscopy, resector balloon deobstruction, 
      and intratumoral chemotherapy, are performed through a rigid or flexible 
      bronchoscope in palliating or curing symptomatic malignant and benign airway 
      lesions to improve symptoms, quality of life, and survival. Technical factors 
      together with patient- and lesion-specific features determine the therapy of 
      choice, as each therapy is different in capacity, limitation, and complications. 
      In this article, indications, contraindications, and complications of 
      endobronchial ablative therapies as well as practical issues related to their 
      rational and cost-effective use are reviewed.
