TI  - A 53-Year-Old Man With a Bronchial Mass and Multiple Bone Lesions.
PG  - e115-e119
LID - S0012-3692(17)31174-1 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.chest.2017.06.018 [doi]
AB  - A 53-year-old man was admitted with complaints of back pain of 3 months' duration 
      along with numbness and weakness in his left upper and lower extremities. He 
      denied any respiratory complaints or anorexia but did report an 11 kg weight loss 
      over the last 3 months. He had no other significant medical history and denied 
      any history of cigarette smoking or recreational drug use. Family history was 
      significant for prostate cancer in his father.
