TI  - Robotic epiglottopexy for severe epiglottic prolapse limiting decannulation.
PG  - 157-159
LID - S0165-5876(17)30453-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ijporl.2017.09.020 [doi]
AB  - Surgical management of supraglottic collapse at the level of the epiglottis 
      limiting decannulation has historically consisted of placement of epiglottopexy 
      sutures which are technically challenging and often unsuccessful. Herein we 
      describe the use of robotic technology to assist with epiglottopexy for a case of 
      a 9 year old child with severe epiglottic petiole prolapse limiting capping and 
      decannulation. Postoperatively the patient is tolerating capping during waking 
      hours.
