TI  - [Hyponatremia in a 58-year-old female patient with EGFR-positive lung 
      adenocarcinoma].
PG  - 384-387
LID - 10.1007/s00108-017-0321-1 [doi]
AB  - The case of a 58-year old female patient with epidermal growth factor-positive 
      pulmonary adenocarcinoma treated with the tyrosine kinase inhibitor afatinib is 
      reported. After several months of first-line therapy the patient developed severe 
      hyponatremia and tumor reassessment revealed a progressive course of the lung 
      cancer. Rebiopsy showed transformation of the tumor into small-cell lung cancer. 
      Therapy with afatinib was stopped immediately and platin-based chemotherapy was 
      started. This case shows that tumor transformation under tyrosine kinase 
      inhibitor therapy from non-small-cell into small-cell lung cancer can occur in 
      rare cases.
