TI  - Aspiration of Nasopore nasal packing.
LID - bcr-2017-221969 [pii]
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2017-221969 [doi]
LID - bcr2017221969
AB  - We present a case of postoperative Nasopore aspiration in an otherwise fit and 
      well 11-year-old. An endoscopic adenoidectomy had been performed without incident 
      and Nasopore packing placed into each nasal cavity. Immediately after extubation, 
      there was marked hypoxia, tachypnoea and high clinical suspicion of pack 
      aspiration. The patient returned to theatre for emergency rigid bronchoscopy and 
      retrieval of nasal packing.
