TI  - Functional airway obstruction observed with hyperpolarized (129) Xenon-MRI.
PG  - 91-93
LID - 10.1111/1754-9485.12660 [doi]
AB  - Hyperpolarized (129) Xenon-MRI (HP (129) Xe MRI) is an emerging imaging modality 
      that allows assessment of both ventilation and gas transfer. Most research to 
      date has focused on non-malignant pulmonary diseases. However, the capability of 
      evaluating the two primary physiological processes of the lung (ventilation and 
      gas transfer) makes HP (129) Xe MRI a promising imaging modality in the 
      management of patients with lung cancer.
