AB  - A woman in her 50s with no significant medical history presented with low-grade 
      fever and cough of 3 days' duration, which was productive of blood-streaked 
      sputum. She was an active smoker, with a 30 pack-year history of smoking. She 
      denied chest pain, chronic cough, exertional dyspnea, or constitutional symptoms.
