DP  - 2018 Jan
TI  - Intact endobronchial hydatid cyst: an unexpected bronchoscopic challenge.
PG  - 60-62
LID - 10.1177/0218492317705287 [doi]
AB  - We describe a rare case of intact endobronchial hydatid cyst that posed a 
      diagnostic challenge because of an unusual imaging manifestation (atelectasis) 
      and unexpected bronchoscopic findings. Although the role of bronchoscopy in the 
      management of pulmonary hydatid cyst is still controversial, 6 cases of 
      complicated pulmonary hydatid cyst removed completely by suction through a 
      fiberoptic bronchoscope have been reported so far. To the best of our knowledge, 
      this is the first nonsurgically treated case of intact endobronchial hydatid cyst 
      with an uneventful long-term follow-up.
