LID - 10.1097/PEC.0000000000000842 [doi]
AB  - Point-of-care ultrasound (POCUS) continues to generate new and interesting 
      clinical findings as its use expands in the pediatric emergency department. This 
      case report describes the novel findings identified during a POCUS focused lung 
      examination of a pediatric patient with suspected foreign body aspiration.
