TI  - Mediastinitis and Bronchial Perforations Due to Mucormycosis.
PG  - 338-42
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0000000000000170 [doi]
AB  - Diabetes mellitus is the most common predisposing condition for mucormycosis, 
      which is emerging as an important invasive fungal infection worldwide. Isolated 
      mediastinitis is a very rare presentation of mucormycosis. A 57-year-old woman 
      with uncontrolled type 2 diabetes mellitus and ketoacidosis presented with septic 
      shock and was subsequently found to have mucor mediastinitis with multiple 
      bronchial perforations. The organism was identified as Rhizopus oryzae with the 
      help of DNA sequencing.
