TI  - Case Report: Pulmonary Papillomatosis in a Patient Presenting with Cough and 
      Hemoptysis.
PG  - e125-7
LID - 10.7812/TPP/14-192 [doi]
AB  - A previously healthy patient was seen in the Emergency Department for evaluation 
      of a one-month history of cough and one-day history of hemoptysis. A computed 
      tomography scan of the thorax found a mass on the right lower pulmonary lobe and 
      a mass on the left upper lobe. A biopsy specimen of the right lobe lung mass, 
      obtained during bronchoscopy, demonstrated papilloma. This case report, from a 
      pulmonologist's perspective, includes a comprehensive review of the patient's 
      clinical presentation and outcome, as well as a discussion of recurrent 
      respiratory papillomatosis.
