AB  - Percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy is a common procedure in intensive care. 
      This updated Danish national guideline describes indications, contraindications 
      and complications, and gives recommendations for timing, anaesthesia, and 
      technique, use of fibre bronchoscopy and ultrasound guidance, as well as 
      decannulation strategy, training, and education.
