TI  - Aspiration of an interesting foreign body: Myiasis.
PG  - 621-623
AB  - Myiasis is a rare condition caused by the invasion of tissues by the larvae of 
      flies. Many cases of myiasis involving various human organs have been reported. 
      Tracheopulmonary or intratracheal myiasis is a very unusual and aberrant form of 
      the disease in humans. We present a case of respiratory myiasis after aspiration 
      of larvae by a healthy 8-month-old girl, which cannot be found in the English 
      literature.
