TI  - Novel Maneuver for Endobronchial Fogarty Embolectomy Catheter Placement for Lung 
      Isolation in Infants: An Experience of Four Cases.
PG  - 541-3
LID - 10.1055/s-0034-1383429 [doi]
AB  - One-lung anesthesia in infant is always a challenge to the pediatric 
      anesthesiologist. Thoracoscopic diaphragmatic eventration repair requires high 
      quality of lung isolation for proper surgical access. We are reporting a new 
      technique of lung isolation by Fogarty embolectomy catheter alongside the 
      endotracheal tube in four infants.
